    class_name: "EffectSummaryIncompleteAtFunctionValue" as NonEmptyStr,
    ceiling: WallAfterGrounding {
      missing_capability: "effect evidence carried on function types -- an effect row in the function's own type. A call through a function value chooses its callee at runtime, so the caller's summary can be exact only when the function TYPE declares the effects any inhabitant may have and the call joins that row; v1.compiler.infer_service's note on the arm records that today the fact is not knowable at the function that carries the call. The check itself is decidable -- the incompleteness marker is present or not -- but promoting now would refuse every call through a function value, ordinary code that is right but unproven (the fabricated-refusal arm DESIGN 4b forbids). Until the row exists the published summary is honestly a lower bound and this diagnostic is the boundary marker, not a defect queue."
    },
    census: DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "gunbc.instrument_targets",
      decl_name: "compile_clean_diagnostic_census_binding",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    }
  },
  AdvisoryClassCeilingRow {
    class_name: "EffectSummaryIncompleteAtLocalBinding" as NonEmptyStr,
    ceiling: WallAfterGrounding {
      missing_capability: "the effect registry's join through local bindings. A call to a local binding's value should read the summary the binding's own initializer established; the registry is keyed by callable identity and does not reach local bindings, so the join contributes nothing and the caller's summary is published as a lower bound. Decidable -- the marker is present or not -- but promoting now would refuse ordinary calls through locally-bound functions that are right but unproven. Where the binding's value is itself a runtime-chosen function this row degrades to the function-value row's capability, and the two burn down together."
    },
    census: DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "gunbc.instrument_targets",
      decl_name: "compile_clean_diagnostic_census_binding",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    }
  }
]

// THE ROSTER PROJECTION THE CENSUS PRODUCER'S BIJECTION WITNESS READS. The host runs this through
// the interpreter over the policy's own closure (the same read path as
// compile_clean_unlisted_import_use_blocks) and checks the roster against the observed population
// and the class schema: no duplicate rows, no row naming a class the schema does not know or whose
// disposition is no longer advisory, and no observed advisory class without a row. A read failure
// is DiagnosticCensusPolicyUnreadable -- the census refuses rather than reporting an unpoliced
// population as an empty one.
fn advisory_ceiling_roster_class_names() -> List<String> {
  advisory_class_ceilings |> map(r => r.class_name as String)
}
